This formula arises from the conservation of energy and momentum within the framework of General Relativity, specifically for a homogeneous and isotropic universe described by the Friedmann-Lemaître-Robertson-Walker (FLRW) metric. It is derived from the fluid equation (or continuity equation) which is a direct consequence of the divergence-free nature of the stress-energy tensor (
\(\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} = 0\)
), representing the local conservation of energy and momentum in an expanding spacetime. This conservation law is rooted in the diffeomorphism invariance (general coordinate invariance) of the theory.
